From 26d707ae256d4f4329aea4b3ff94a20c0cca745e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brhett <36874370+jingledingle521@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:52:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 42/42] Finder: sidebar drag and drop, slide-out sidebar,
 iCloud Drive
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Sidebar:
- Drop folders between Favorites to pin them (insertion line), drag
  Favorites to reorder them, and drop files onto an item to move or copy
  them into it (Dolphin's drop menu). Trash trashes them, cloud drives
  upload them, and AirDrop opens the share sheet.
- Icons, drop line and drop outline use the system accent.
- View › Hide/Show Sidebar (Ctrl+Alt+S), worded as on macOS.
- With the sidebar hidden, resting the pointer on the window's left
  edge (14 px) slides it out over the content as a floating panel. It
  slides away once a place is picked or the pointer leaves it.

Cloud drives: FinderCloud is now one instance per provider. iCloud
Drive joins Google Drive, run by rclone's iclouddrive backend.
- Sign-in uses the Apple ID and password (SRP, as icloud.com does; the
  password goes through `rclone obscure` on stdin, never argv), then
  the 2FA code from a trusted device or a text, driven through rclone's
  non-interactive config protocol.
- Mounted at ~/iCloud Drive by finder-icloud-drive.service, listed
  under its own iCloud heading above Locations.
- An expired trust token (30 days) shows as signed out, with Sign In
  Again.
- Each drive keeps its own config file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
